<title>USA: Kroger sets stock repurchase program.</title>
<headline>Kroger sets stock repurchase program.</headline>
<dateline>CINCINNATI 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kroger Co said Wednesday it would begin repurchasing an unspecified amount of its stock to reduce dilution caused by its stock option plans for employees.</p>
<p>The repurchase program will be funded by proceeds from employee stock option exercises, plus associated tax benefits, Kroger said.</p>
<p>If the repurchase program had been in effect in 1996, about $70 million in proceeds from option exercises would have been available for stock buybacks, it said.</p>
</text>
